From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a sandboxed frame asking for a passkey is not a
 crash

A sandboxed frame calling
PublicKeyCredential.isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() took
the desktop down: content's GetWebAuthnRequestProxyIfActive DCHECKs that
the caller's origin is not opaque, and IsUVPAA and getClientCapabilities
call it before anything checks the origin. create() and get() validate
it first. A fraud-detection script on a real site asked from one, and the
checked engine aborted.

An opaque origin has no webAuthenticationProxy -- an extension takes an
origin's requests, and nothing can name an opaque one -- so the lookup
answers none and the request goes on as any other: patch 0048's IsUVPAA
override answers false.
---
 content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc b/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
index 7b6004e712..bd7a62ddcf 100644
--- a/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/webauth/authenticator_common_impl.cc
@@ -3543,6 +3543,14 @@ void AuthenticatorCommonImpl::EnableRequestProxyExtensionsAPISupport() {
 WebAuthenticationRequestProxy*
 AuthenticatorCommonImpl::GetWebAuthnRequestProxyIfActive(
     const url::Origin& caller_origin) {
+  // Domicile's engine fork: an opaque origin has no proxy, because an
+  // extension takes an origin's requests and nothing can name this one. A
+  // sandboxed frame's isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticatorAvailable() and
+  // getClientCapabilities() reach here unchecked, and a DCHECK aborted the
+  // browser on them. See upstream/webauthn-opaque-origin-proxy-dcheck.md.
+  if (caller_origin.opaque()) {
+    return nullptr;
+  }
   // The Virtual Authenticator, which can be activated via Dev Tools UI or
   // ChromeDriver, should take precedence over request proxying. Otherwise
   // attaching a remote desktop session would interfere with automated or manual
